# iDroid HUD

Puente looks like the MGSV iDroid: cyan hairline panels on navy, dense rows, one dossier. Tokens and screen patterns live in `docs/PLAN.md` § Visual system. Use the CSS variables. Do not add a second palette.

## Patterns — pick one, do not invent

- **Roster** — transactions, bills, import diff, audit.
- **Grade cards** — the three buckets, and Conservative / Base / Optimistic.
- **Requirements** — required vs current (savings rule, “can I buy?”, card vs bank).
- **Dossier + stat bars** — Disponible real breakdown, card detail, scenario result, spend by type.
- **Series** — expense over time and unit price by date. One cyan line. Amber is the previous window only. Heat marks over-budget, not a category. No rainbow charts and no extra chart palette.
- **Command bar** — tabs and verbs. Add is a `+` verb, not a shadowed floating button. Estadísticas and Precios are views on Movimientos, not new tabs.

Phone: status strip, stage, command bar. The dossier is a right column when wide and a sheet when narrow.

## Color means one thing

- `--cyan` / `--cyan-bright` — safe, progress, the hero number.
- `--amber` — tight, locked, warning.
- `--heat` — shortfall and over-pace bars.
- `--ink-dim` — the one-line footer hint.

Radius stays `--radius` (2px). No drop shadows, no purple, no large rounded finance cards.

## Type and money

- Labels: 11px uppercase, wide tracking.
- Amounts and dates: tabular mono, `es-MX`, with `MXN` or `CAD` visible.
- One hero figure per screen. Inicio’s question is “¿Cuánto tengo de verdad?”.

Styling is plain CSS in `src/App.css` and `src/styles/tokens.css`. Reuse the components in `src/components/hud.tsx` and `fields.tsx` before adding classes.

```tsx
// ❌ new card chrome
<div style={{ borderRadius: 16, boxShadow: '0 8px 24px #0004', color: '#10b981' }}>

// ✅ existing HUD pieces
<Panel title="Tarjetas de crédito">
  <StatBar label="− Deuda TDC" value={formatMoney(debt, 'MXN')} ratio={debt / scale} />
</Panel>
```
